[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 764,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 701,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119666,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 339,
        "headingId": 701,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma (B-ALL/LBL) with <em>TCF3</em>::<em>PBX1</em> fusion is a neoplasm of lymphoblasts of B-cell lineage defined by the presence of rearrangement between <em>TCF3</em> on chromosome&nbsp;19 and <em>PBX1</em> on chromosome&nbsp;1.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:29:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 765,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 702,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119667,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 339,
        "headingId": 702,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>9818/3 B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma with <em>TCF3</em>::<em>PBX1</em> fusion</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:29:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 766,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 703,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119668,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 339,
        "headingId": 703,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>2A70.Y &amp; XH3GU8 Other B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma with recurrent genetic abnormalities &amp; B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma with t(1;19)(q23;p13.3); <em>E2A</em>-<em>PBX1</em> (<em>TCF3</em>-<em>PBX1</em>)</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:29:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 767,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 704,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119669,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 339,
        "headingId": 704,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma with <em>E2A</em>::<em>PBX1</em>.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:29:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 768,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 705,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119670,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 339,
        "headingId": 705,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:29:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 769,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 706,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119671,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 339,
        "headingId": 706,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>B-ALL and B-LBL represent the same disease. B-ALL always involves the bone marrow and usually also involves the peripheral blood. Extramedullary involvement is common and is by definition the primary site of involvement in B-LBL. For details, see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/63/385\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma</em> .</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:29:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 770,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 707,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119672,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 339,
        "headingId": 707,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>There are no unique features (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/63/108\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>B-lymphoblastic leukaemias/lymphomas: Introduction</em>).</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:29:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 771,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 708,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119673,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 339,
        "headingId": 708,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>B-ALL/LBL with <em>TCF3</em>::<em>PBX1</em> fusion is relatively common in children, accounting for approximately 5% of paediatric B-ALL/LBL cases, and it is rare in adults {19713226}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:29:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 772,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 709,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119674,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 339,
        "headingId": 709,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:29:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 773,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 710,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119675,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 339,
        "headingId": 710,
        "headingText": "<p>The <em>TCF3</em>::<em>PBX1</em> fusion, usually resulting from t(1;19)(q23;q13.3), has been identified in 0.6% of healthy newborns {31434706}, suggesting that like <em>ETV6</em>::<em>RUNX1</em>, <em>TCF3</em>::<em>PBX1</em> is an early lesion necessary but not sufficient for leukaemogenesis. The <em>TCF3</em>::<em>PBX1</em> fusion results in the production of a fusion protein that has an oncogenic role as a transcriptional activator; it also probably interferes with the normal function of the transcription factors encoded by <em>TCF3</em>&nbsp;and <em>PBX1</em> {12700034}. Gene expression profiling studies have identified a signature unique to this lesion {12086872}, and <em>PHF6</em> mutations have been described {33095873}. Downstream WNT signalling and PI3K abnormalities have been implicated in pathogenesis {27461063; 30631148}.</p>\r\n&nbsp;",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-21T11:54:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 780,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 717,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119676,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 339,
        "headingId": 717,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:29:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 774,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 711,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119677,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 339,
        "headingId": 711,
        "headingText": "<p>There are no unique morphological features.</p>\r\n\r\n<h5>Immunophenotype</h5>\r\n\r\n<p>The abnormal B&nbsp;lymphoblasts show strong CD9 expression, dim to negative CD34 expression, and at least partial absence of CD20, in addition to CD19 and CD10 expression {8353275; 28187514}. Cytoplasmic mu heavy chain expression is frequently present but not entirely specific for this entity {28187514}.</p>\r\n&nbsp;",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:30:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 775,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 712,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119678,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 339,
        "headingId": 712,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>No unique features</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:29:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 776,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 713,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119679,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 339,
        "headingId": 713,
        "headingText": "<p>The <em>TCF3</em>::<em>PBX1</em> fusion is detectable by karyotype, FISH, and molecular methods {17311319; 32150610}. The functional fusion gene resides on chromosome&nbsp;19, and there may be loss of the derivative chromosome&nbsp;1 in a majority of cases, resulting in an unbalanced translocation on karyotype analysis. Molecular methods may help identify cryptic translocations {34460133} as well as alternate fusion partners {31575852}.</p>\r\n<p>Importantly, B-ALL/LBL with <em>TCF3</em> partners other than <em>PBX1</em> are not included in this entity. <em>TCF3</em> break-apart FISH is not sufficient, as this will not distinguish between <em>TCF3</em>::<em>PBX1</em> and <em>TCF3</em>::<em>HLF</em>. B-ALL/LBL with <em>TCF3</em>::<em>HLF</em>&nbsp;rearrangement carries a poor prognosis and is classified separately. In addition, cases of B-ALL/LBL, commonly with hyperdiploidy, have a karyotypically identical t(1;19) that involves neither <em>TCF3</em> nor <em>PBX1</em> and should not be classified as B-ALL/LBL with <em>TCF3</em>::<em>PBX1</em> fusion.</p>\r\n&nbsp;",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-21T11:14:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 779,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 716,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119680,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 339,
        "headingId": 716,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> meets the diagnostic criteria for B-ALL/LBL (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/63/385\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma</em>); demonstration of <em>TCF3</em>::<em>PBX1</em> rearrangement.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:29:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 777,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 714,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119681,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 339,
        "headingId": 714,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:29:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 778,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 715,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119682,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 339,
        "headingId": 715,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>With modern intensive therapy, B-ALL/LBL with <em>TCF3</em>::<em>PBX1</em> fusion is associated with intermediate to relatively favourable clinical outcomes {19713226; 21534874; 30051646; 32955970; 33221150; 33895809; 34250504; 34406703; 34549416}. However, there may be an increased relative risk of CNS relapse in these patients {19282835}. Relapsed patients appear to have a dismal prognosis.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:29:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]